WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.360
- [Instructor] In this video

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.250
we're going to think about
how fractions can be used

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.240
to represent things in the real world.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.000
So here we're told that
on the Sharks dive team

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.810
there are three divers in third grade.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.000
There are eight total divers on the team.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
What fraction of Sharks
dive team is in third grade?

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.383
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.540
All right, so first of all they tell us

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.170
there are eight total divers on the team.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.800
So maybe I'll represent each diver

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.500
with a little circle like this,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.120
I'll try to make it look
kind of like a diver,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.890
so that's not quite a
circle but you get the idea,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.410
it looks like something
kind of diving down.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.410
So one, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, and eight.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.350
Now if we were to talk
about just one diver here,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.720
just like that, that would
be one out of the eight.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.240
Or we would often call that one eighth,

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.210
so eight with a h at the end.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.120
That is one eighth right over there,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.580
or I could represent it like this,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.443
I could say this is an eighth, an eighth,

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:14.030
or I could say that this is equal to 1/8.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.030
This is one of the eight
members of our dive team.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.480
Now they tell us that there are
three divers in third grade,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.410
what fraction of Sharks
dive team is in third grade?

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.760
So that is, let's say it these three,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.946
so there's three out of the eight.

00:01:32.946 --> 00:01:35.640
So if you wanted to
represent that as a fraction

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.773
you could represent it as 3/8 like this,

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.900
or you could represent it as,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.830
if you wanted to write it out as a word,

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.570
three, instead of having
it three over eight,

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.560
you could write three eighths like that.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.610
If you were doing this on Khan Academy

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.030
there'd be some choices out there

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.980
where you'd pick one
of the correct choice,

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.310
but you could represent the
fraction of Sharks dive team

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.676
that is in third grade either
as three over eight, 3/8,

00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:07.260
or three and then spell
out the word eighths.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.510
Let's do another example.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.800
Here we are told Yuma divided his clay

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.410
into four equal parts.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.410
He made clay animals out
of three of the parts.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:27.100
What fraction of the clay did
Yuma use to make clay animals?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.250
So one again, pause this
video, and think about it.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.510
All right, so let's just imagine

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.940
that this is his clay, initially,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.660
and he divides it into four equal parts.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:41.490
And so let's say he divides it like this.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.480
And let's say that I've divided
it into four equal parts,

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.260
that these all have the
exact amount of clay in it,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.250
it's hand drawn so it's
not going to be perfect

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.540
the way I drew it but
let's assume they all have

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.363
the exact same amount of clay.

00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:54.690
Now it says that he made clay animals

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.923
out of three of the parts.

00:02:56.923 --> 00:02:59.530
So maybe, this part right over here,

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.468
he was able to make a clay animal out of,

00:03:01.468 --> 00:03:04.404
this part right over here,
he made a clay animal out of,

00:03:04.404 --> 00:03:06.520
and then that part, right over there,

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.264
he made a clay animal out of.

00:03:08.264 --> 00:03:09.910
So what fraction of the clay

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.392
did he use to make clay animals?

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.730
So what would you call
each of the equal parts?

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.080
So if I were to just focus
on that right over there,

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.870
you would call that a fourth, a fourth.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.700
You could also represent it
as one fourth, like that,

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.420
or you could represent it as 1/4.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.440
That's if you were to just
circle one of these equal parts,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.074
that one, or that one,
or that one, or that one.

00:03:35.074 --> 00:03:37.490
Now if you're talking
about all of his clay,

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:38.440
what are you talking about?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.810
Well you could view it as
four fourths, four fourths,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.450
or four over four, this would
also be read four fourths.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.283
That would be referring to

00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:50.370
all one, two, three, four of his clay.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.460
Now if you wanted to say
what fraction of the clay

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.620
did Yuma use to make clay animals,

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.710
we can see that three of the fourths,

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.080
were used to make clay animals.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.210
So to answer that question,

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.240
we would say three of the fourths,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.080
so three fourths were
used to make clay animals.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.080
You can also express that as a fraction.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.020
You could also write
that as 3/4 like this.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.550
You would read these the same,

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.520
three fourths, or three fourths.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.274
Three out of the four
equal sections of clay

00:04:24.274 --> 00:04:27.653
were used to make the clay animals.

